# Names to show for desktop entries that come from a port's own tarball.
#
# Most entries in /usr/share/applications are written here (xterm.desktop,
# xcalc.desktop, netsurf.desktop) and say whatever this file says.  Three come
# from the packages themselves, installed into the sysroot by their own `make
# install', and this is where those are given the names this desktop uses.
#
# Renaming rather than overriding.  A replacement .desktop file would have to
# repeat the upstream Exec, Icon, MimeType, Categories, Keywords and Actions
# lines, and every one of those is a thing to get wrong now and a thing to
# forget on the next version bump.  Only the Name is ours; everything else
# stays exactly as the package installed it.
#
# The names matter because two pairs of programs would otherwise collide in
# the menu.  Galculator and xcalc are both "Calculator"; xfce4-terminal and
# xterm are both "Terminal".  In each pair the newer program takes the plain
# name and the X.Org one is qualified, which is the way round a user expects:
# "Terminal" is the one to open, "Xterm" is the one you ask for by name.
#
# Applied by ports/xorg/gtk3/stage.sh after it copies the sysroot's entries,
# which is the only moment both halves are in one directory.  The desktop
# shortcuts in /etc/skel/Desktop carry the same names, written out there.
#
# Format: the .desktop file name, whitespace, then the name to show.  Blank
# lines and # comments are ignored.  Localised Name[xx]= lines are left alone;
# a user running in a language the package was translated into gets the
# translation, which is the right outcome and is what the untouched file
# already does.

galculator.desktop        Calculator
xfce4-terminal.desktop    Terminal
io.github.Hexchat.desktop Hexchat IRC Client
